# Additional Permission: GSTD Network Participation and Applications

The PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 above remains unmodified. In addition,
the licensor grants the following permission, to the extent it controls the
relevant rights, to individuals and legal entities, including companies. These
additional terms do not limit rights already granted by PolyForm above; its
permitted noncommercial uses remain available without relying on this permission.

1. **Commercial participation and applications.** You may use, modify,
   distribute, embed and host the covered software and extensions to it to
   participate in the GSTD network as an operator, worker or client, and to
   build and offer applications and integrations using that network. This
   includes commercial applications and receiving GSTD for accepted work.
   Keep the license terms and required notices with distributed covered code.

2. **Paid network compute uses GSTD.** When relying on this additional
   permission to provide paid distributed-compute services through the covered
   core software or a commercial extension to it, settle those compute charges
   in canonical GSTD. Canonical GSTD on TON mainnet has token-master address
   `0:efe9c616f673622a337737097c0fa0018d4887d6061f59519985f3fbfbdb59b2`.
   GSTD-denominated reservations and accounting may represent underlying GSTD;
   they do not authorize issuing substitute tokens or representing unfunded
   balances as redeemable GSTD. Test-network fixtures are not real payments.

3. **Narrow payment condition.** The GSTD settlement condition applies only to
   those paid network-compute charges. Bundling covered paid network compute
   into another charge does not remove the GSTD settlement condition for the
   underlying compute. It does not require unrelated business
   fees, subscriptions, consulting, support or other independent products to
   be priced or paid in GSTD. This permission imposes no token-payment
   requirement for installation, local-only execution, free requests or model
   downloads. Normal blockchain gas and network fees may be paid in TON or
   the native network asset; they are not GSTD compute charges.

4. **Other commercial core uses.** Commercial sale or licensing of the covered
   core software for uses outside the participation and application permission
   above, including a separate commercial network that does not satisfy its
   GSTD compute-settlement condition, requires a separate written license.
   This does not restrict rights independently granted by another license.

5. **Independent implementations and SDKs.** This permission does not impose
   conditions on independent implementations, unrelated software or the use of
   public interfaces without incorporating covered code. Separately licensed
   SDKs and clients remain governed by their own licenses; using an Apache-2.0
   SDK does not itself impose a GSTD payment obligation.

6. **Third-party rights.** Third-party code, dependencies, models and assets
   retain their own licenses and notices. This permission neither relicenses
   them nor grants rights the licensor does not control. Token settlement does
   not replace model-license or other third-party obligations.

7. **Earlier releases and no service promise.** Earlier copies retain the
   licenses under which they were released. No retroactive condition is added.
   This permission grants software rights, not token value, guaranteed work,
   earnings, service availability or an activated payment mechanism.

The covered core remains source-available, not OSI open source. The additional
payment condition is not part of the unmodified PolyForm license itself.
